# Upload only what apps/web/Dockerfile actually COPYs, via
#   gcloud builds submit --config cloudbuild.web.yaml --ignore-file=.gcloudignore.web .
# Companion to the root .gcloudignore, which is written for the API image
# only (it excludes apps/ entirely). Without this file, a plain
# `gcloud builds submit` from repo root uploads the whole tree, including
# every node_modules and .next across the monorepo.
#
# Re-including a path nested under an excluded directory does not work in
# gitignore syntax ("it is not possible to re-include a file if a parent
# directory of that file is excluded") — `/*` then `!apps/web/` alone
# silently drops everything under apps/, contents included. Verified: an
# earlier version of this file written that way passed
# `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload` with only the 4 top-level files
# listed below and none of apps/web's own source. So each directory level is
# un-ignored explicitly, shallowest first, before narrowing back down.
/*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!cloudbuild.web.yaml

!apps/
apps/*
!apps/web/
!apps/news/
apps/news/*
!apps/news/package.json

!packages/
packages/*
!packages/ts/
packages/ts/*
!packages/ts/ui/
!packages/ts/contracts-gen/
!packages/ts/ui-visual/
packages/ts/ui-visual/*
!packages/ts/ui-visual/package.json
# packages/py/ stays excluded: `packages/*` above only un-ignores packages/ts.

# Build artefacts and caches — never needed as input, and node_modules alone
# is the bulk of what the root .gcloudignore exists to keep out of the API
# upload too. These apply INSIDE the now-included apps/web and packages/ts
# trees; excluding within an included directory is the ordinary case and
# does not hit the re-inclusion trap above.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.next-*/
**/.turbo/
**/.vercel/
**/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/.venv.nosync/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Secrets and local-only files. `apps/web/.gitignore` already keeps these out
# of git, but this is a separate upload path with its own rules — repeated
# here rather than assumed, per 05-security.md's supply-chain stance on
# never letting a credential ride along with a build context.
.env*
**/.env*
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
